  "result": "`click.KeyValue` is added, and the full test suite passes (1912 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed). I didn't run the manual `python -c` check from the plan.\n\n- **Behavior:** `KeyValue` splits on the first `=` and returns `(key, value)`. `a=b=c` gives `(\"a\", \"b=c\")`, and `a=` gives `(\"a\", \"\")`. Input with no `=` or an empty key fails with `'ab' is not a valid key=value pair.` I confirmed this wording in the new test.\n- **Code and tests:** The class is in `src/click/types.py` and exported from `src/click/__init__.py`. I added `test_key_value_option` to `tests/test_basic.py`. It covers the good cases, both failure cases, and `multiple=True`.\n- **Docs:** I added entries in `docs/api.md` and `docs/parameter-types.md`. `CHANGES.md` has a new \"Version 8.6.0 / Unreleased\" section, since 8.5.0 is already released.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
